  "units": [
    {
      "id": "p74221_6_naming_methods",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [2, 3],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "R2C--O+=O <-> R2C=O+-O-. Method (1) in P-74.2.2.1 gives preferred IUPAC names."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p74221_7_naming_methods",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [8, 9],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "R2C=O+-C-(R)2 <-> R2C+-OC-(R)2. Method (2) in P-74.2.2.1 gives preferred IUPAC names."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p74221_8_naming_methods",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [14, 15],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "RR'C=S+-O- <-> RR'C=S=O, where R' = or != H. Method (4) in P-74.2.2.1 gives preferred IUPAC names."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p74221_9_naming_methods",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [24, 25, 26],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "R2C=N+(O-)R' <-> R2C+-N(O-)R' where R' != H; compounds where R' = H are not included in this class. Method (3) in P-74.2.2.1 gives preferred IUPAC names."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p74221_10_nitro_compound_mapping",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "required",
      "c": [33, 34],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "The example maps the displayed nitro compound to nitroethane (PIN)."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p74222_dipolar_atom_combinations",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "required",
      "c": [36, 37],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "X triple-bond N+--Z- <-> -X=N+=Z <-> -X=N-Z+, where X = C, N or O and Z = C, N or O."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p742221_naming_methods",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [39, 40],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "Name these compounds either as zwitterionic compounds without breaking the longest chain of heteroatoms, or by functional class nomenclature using the class names imide, oxide, sulfide, etc."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p7422211_zwitterionic_names",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [42],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "Method (1) in P-74.2.2.2.1, zwitterionic names, generates preferred IUPAC names."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p7422212_functional_class_names",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [47],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "Method (2) in P-74.2.2.2.1, functional class names, yields preferred IUPAC names (see also P-66.5.4.1)."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p7422213_zwitterionic_names",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [54],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "Method (1) in P-74.2.2.2.1, zwitterionic names, gives preferred IUPAC names."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p742222_azide_naming_methods",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [59, 60, 61, 62],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "Azides may be named by three methods: (1) substitutively, using the compulsory prefix azido (P-61.7); (2) by functional class nomenclature using the class name azide; (3) as derivatives of the zwitterionic parent hydride 'triazadien-2-ium-1-ide.' Method (1) yields preferred IUPAC names (see also P-61.7)."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p742223_diazo_naming_methods",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [67, 68, 69],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "Diazo compounds may be named in two ways: (1) substitutively by using the compulsory prefix diazo (P-61.4); (2) as derivatives of the zwitterionic parent hydride diazen-2-ium-1-ide. Method (1) leads to preferred IUPAC names (see also P-61.4)."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p74223_delocalized_carbene_form",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "required",
      "c": [74],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "X2 radical-C=Z <-> +X=C-Z-, where X = C or N and Z = C, N or O."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p742231_ylidene_example_rule",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [77],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "The displayed delocalized carbene is named using the ylidene form as the preferred IUPAC name."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p742232_imidoyl_carbene_naming",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [80, 81, 82, 83, 84, 85],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "Compounds having the structure RC(=NH)-C2 radical-R are imidoyl carbenes. Imidoyl is a shortened, but imprecise, term for carboximidoyl, RC(=NH)-. These carbenes may be named by two methods: (1) by using the longest carbon chain, according to the principles of substitutive nomenclature for radicals, low locants being assigned to the radical to be cited as suffix; (2) substitutively on the basis of the appropriate carbene as the parent structure. Method (1) leads to preferred IUPAC names."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p742233_azanylidene_nitrene_aminylene_naming",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [90, 91, 92],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "RC(=N-R')N2 radical <-> RC(N--R')=N+. They may be named substitutively using the parent names azanylidene, nitrene, or aminylene. The use of 'azanylidene' leads to preferred IUPAC names."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p742234_longest_chain_ylidene_naming",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "preference",
      "c": [97],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "Preferred IUPAC names are formed by using the longest carbon chain according to the principles of substitutive nomenclature for radicals, low locants being assigned to the suffix 'ylidene'."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p7423_dipolar_substituent_group_naming",
      "k": "procedure",
      "f": "required",
      "c": [102],
      "steps": [
        ["emit", "Names of dipolar substituent groups are formed by using prefixes for naming ions as the substituent group and designating the free valences by the suffixes 'yl', 'ylidene' or 'ylidyne'."]
      ]
    }
  ],
